Chapter: Arith
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A small Codex program with answers you can check by hand.

 It exists so that "the transpiler really transpiles" is something you can
 verify rather than take on faith. Not one of the numbers it prints appears
 anywhere in this source: 42, 92, 610, 5050 and 63 are all computed, and 92
 is computed by backtracking search over a chessboard. A transpiler that
 echoed its input, or emitted a fixed prelude, could not produce them.

 Run `./build.py` and it transpiles, builds and runs this, then compares the
 output to samples/arith.expected. The zig it produced is kept beside it, in
 generated/arith.zig, so you can read what it actually emitted.

Section: Recursion

  fib : Integer -> Integer
  fib (n) = if n < 2 then n else fib (n - 1) + fib (n - 2)

  sum-to : Integer -> Integer
  sum-to (n) = if n == 0 then 0 else n + sum-to (n - 1)

Section: Higher Order

  triple : Integer -> Integer
  triple = (\x -> x * 3)

  twice : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  twice (f) (x) = f (f x)

Section: Matching

  size-of : Integer -> Text
  size-of (n) = when n
    is 0 -> "none"
    is 1 -> "one"
    is otherwise -> if n < 10 then "few" else "many"

Section: Bounded Integers

  Score = record {
    v : Integer between 0 and 100 clamping
  }

Section: Eight Queens

 Backtracking, column by column. `placed` holds the row of each queen already
 placed, most recent first, so the queen at index i is exactly i + 1 columns
 away and a diagonal attack is a row difference equal to that distance.

  q-abs : Integer -> Integer
  q-abs (x) = if x < 0 then -x else x

  q-ok : Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  q-ok (row) (placed) (i) =
    if i == list-length placed then True
    else let r = list-at placed i
      in if r == row then False
      else if q-abs (r - row) == i + 1 then False
      else q-ok row placed (i + 1)

  q-rows : Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  q-rows (row) (placed) =
    if row > 8 then 0
    else let here = if q-ok row placed 0 then q-solve ([row] & placed) else 0
      in here + q-rows (row + 1) placed

  q-solve : List Integer -> Integer
  q-solve (placed) = if list-length placed == 8 then 1 else q-rows 1 placed

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "hello, world"
    print-line-uni ("six-times-seven: " & show (6 * 7))
    print-line-uni ("eight-queens: " & show (q-solve []))
    print-line-uni ("fib-15: " & show (fib 15))
    print-line-uni ("sum-to-100: " & show (sum-to 100))
    print-line-uni ("twice-triple-7: " & show (twice triple 7))
    print-line-uni ("size-of: " & size-of 0 & "/" & size-of 1 & "/" & size-of 5 & "/" & size-of 50)
    print-line-uni ("clamped-250: " & show (Score { v = 250 }).v)
    let xs = [1, 2, 3] & [4, 5]
    in print-line-uni ("list-length: " & show (list-length xs))
  end

